<p>Nepal’s Rastriya Swatantra Party (RSP), led by rapper-turned-politician and former Kathmandu mayor Balendra “Balen” Shah, is on track to form the next government after partial results showed a sweeping win in Saturday’s general election. Several outlets said Shah defeated former prime minister K.P. Sharma Oli in the Jhapa-5 constituency, highlighting the scale of the upset. It was the country’s first parliamentary election since violent, youth-led protests toppled the previous leadership in September. Many reports described the RSP’s rise as a reformist, anti-corruption, anti-establishment wave powered by younger voters. Preliminary turnout was around 60%. If confirmed, Shah would become Nepal’s youngest prime minister and the country’s first Madhesi leader to hold the top job—signaling a generational shift and a change in representation in the Himalayan nation’s politics.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4WCmo0xZTjQFhPjLejLgwPNbfCPVpCQHWJW-9RJLeTYTLLs45q1ZJM9g3VwxGKI8r4XCgfWjZmofBQ5OCI1pBk5lmBRtDfYBDsxe3lsixc-Tb6rmHGv3cgIrjAnkQjs7mgGNGJER837BWalxBcG8Y9edFHjZ0i3L6OPv1py9lb2DYGlLrjGhbsxWZAB-fEvtnc1l4V3wCl_lC2-AslHKpucs' alt='Balendra Shah during his campaign; RSP president Rabi Lamichhane stands nearby.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Seat picture: AP said the RSP had won 60 of 165 first-past-the-post seats and was leading in 61 more constituencies in partial preliminary results.</li><li>Vote margin: The Hindu said Shah received 68,348 votes to Oli’s 18,734 in their contest.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>K.P. Sharma Oli: Oli sent greetings to Balendra Shah after Shah’s win, according to NDTV’s report on his message. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/former-nepal-pm-kp-sharma-oli-extends-greetings-to-balen-shah-on-poll-win-11184094#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Rastriya Swatantra Party: The party campaigned on anti-corruption and anti-establishment themes, The Hindu reported, presenting itself as a reform alternative to traditional politics. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/rastriya-swatantra-party-the-bell-strikes/article70716831.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Younger protest-linked voters: BBC and Al Jazeera tied the RSP’s surge to a youth-driven reform wave after last year’s uprising and the September protests. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c93w6y0lnd9o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Gen Z supporters: The New York Times highlighted Gen Z support for Shah as he headed toward a landslide, underscoring the strength of younger voters in this cycle. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/07/world/asia/nepal-election-rapper-balen-genz.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/former-nepal-pm-kp-sharma-oli-extends-greetings-to-balen-shah-on-poll-win-11184094#publisher=newsstand'>Former Nepal PM KP Sharma Oli Extends Greetings To Balen Shah On Poll Win</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/balendra-shahs-rsp-makes-history-registers-landmark-victory-in-nepal-election/article70718163.ece'>Balendra Shah&#x27;s RSP makes history, registers landmark victory in Nepal election</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c93w6y0lnd9o'>Rapper-politician Balendra Shah unseats Nepal&#x27;s ex-PM as he heads for victory</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/07/world/asia/nepal-election-rapper-balen-genz.html'>Gen Z-Backed Rapper Is on Course to Lead Nepal With Landslide Win</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/8/rapper-turned-politician-defeats-veteran-leader-in-nepal-election-upset'>Rapper-turned-politician Balen Shah’s RSP heads for poll landslide in Nepal</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/new-nepali-party-led-rapper-set-landslide-win-130872077'>A new Nepali party, led by an ex-rapper, is set for a landslide win in parliamentary election</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/nepal-parliament-election-results-balendra-shah-aac242077d2dd052e7e9bdd7c088ccc9'>Partial preliminary results in Nepal indicate that the Rastriya Swatantra Party (RSP) won 60 of 165 first-past-the-post seats, while also leading in 61 other consituencies. In Jhapa 5, RSP prime ministerial candidate Balen Shah defeats former prime minister K. P. Sharma Oli. (AP)</a> - apnews.com</li></ul>